WEBVTT

00:00:18.891 --> 00:00:21.311
Oh! So cool.

00:00:26.903 --> 00:00:28.101
Bottom of the ninth,
tie score.

00:00:28.222 --> 00:00:29.761
And exactly who you want
at the plate

00:00:29.761 --> 00:00:31.462
with the game
on the line: Sonic!

00:00:32.041 --> 00:00:33.842
But staring him down
from the pitcher's mound

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:36.909
is the most fearsome southpaw
in Green Hills:

00:00:37.001 --> 00:00:38.182
Also Sonic.

00:00:38.442 --> 00:00:40.781
Okay. Focus, Sonic.
If you win this game,

00:00:40.781 --> 00:00:42.521
you'll be the most beloved kid
in Green Hills.

00:00:45.163 --> 00:00:46.936
[armpit fart noise]

00:00:47.041 --> 00:00:50.721
Hit it to the guy in left!
He's a real space case.

00:00:53.871 --> 00:00:55.692
[groans]
I can't with that guy.

00:00:55.795 --> 00:00:57.317
Hey, batter Sonic.
Hey, batter Sonic.

00:00:57.422 --> 00:01:00.156
"Suh-wing," batter Sonic.

00:01:05.728 --> 00:01:07.527
[sniffing, gasps]

00:01:07.631 --> 00:01:09.191
I got it, I got it, I got it!

00:01:10.232 --> 00:01:11.232
I don't got it.

00:01:20.515 --> 00:01:22.501
Go home! Go home!

00:01:22.791 --> 00:01:23.791
Come on!

00:01:25.112 --> 00:01:26.616
[yells]

00:01:29.147 --> 00:01:30.147
Safe!

00:01:32.772 --> 00:01:35.352
Yes!
Yes, yes, yes, yes! I did it!

00:01:35.552 --> 00:01:37.792
Did you see that?
I did it. I did it.

00:01:44.532 --> 00:01:47.470
[crickets chirping]

00:01:50.892 --> 00:01:52.432
I really am alone.

00:01:53.892 --> 00:01:55.532
All alone. Forever.

00:02:02.698 --> 00:02:04.826
[electricity crackling]

00:02:13.944 --> 00:02:15.753
[panting]

00:02:16.853 --> 00:02:18.734
[yells]

00:02:28.029 --> 00:02:29.058
[satellite powers down]

00:02:30.442 --> 00:02:33.522
I'm sure no one noticed that
giant blue explosion, right?

00:02:33.983 --> 00:02:36.149
[lines ringing]

00:02:40.163 --> 00:02:42.755
[cell phone rings]

00:02:44.141 --> 00:02:46.242
Hey, Wade.
Hi, Tom.

00:02:46.421 --> 00:02:47.421
Uh, Wade here.
[nervous chuckle]

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.161
What is going on?

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:51.321
Well, gosh,
I think the power's out.

00:02:51.425 --> 00:02:53.236
Yeah, no dur!
The lights are out.

00:02:53.342 --> 00:02:54.821
The whole town is freaking out.

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:57.141
What should I do?
[Tom] Okay, relax.

00:02:57.201 --> 00:02:58.962
Take a deep breath, call Gil,

00:02:59.162 --> 00:03:01.101
see if they can locate
the downed line, then...

00:03:01.882 --> 00:03:04.842
call Zim and see if he can
get his generator
over to the Super Q

00:03:04.842 --> 00:03:06.042
so the food stays... fresh.

00:03:06.161 --> 00:03:09.441
[Wade]
Call Zim before Gil?

00:03:10.242 --> 00:03:11.962
Call Gil-- Hello?
I'll call you back.

00:03:12.022 --> 00:03:13.941
Wait! Hello? Was that
the end of the instructions?

00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:15.960
[phones ringing]

00:03:16.121 --> 00:03:18.781
Okay, all right.
Uh, you can do this.

00:03:20.121 --> 00:03:22.581
What was the first thing
he said to do?

00:03:24.621 --> 00:03:26.702
Right. Relax.

00:03:36.712 --> 00:03:39.413
[electricity crackling]

00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:49.432
Twenty minutes ago,
an energy surge

00:03:49.432 --> 00:03:52.052
knocked out power across
the entire Pacific Northwest.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.052
What do we know?

00:03:53.052 --> 00:03:55.172
Well, our first instinct
was it was an EMP.

00:03:56.507 --> 00:03:58.535
But electromagnetic pulses
don't have that kind of power.

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:01.552
NASA has ruled out
meteor strikes or solar flares.

00:04:01.631 --> 00:04:04.192
The Department of Energy says
it's not a power plant
malfunction.

00:04:04.472 --> 00:04:05.891
Well, sounds like
we're really good

00:04:05.891 --> 00:04:06.992
at figuring out
what it wasn't.

00:04:07.192 --> 00:04:09.631
This could be a prelude
to a larger attack.

00:04:09.911 --> 00:04:11.692
I'm suggesting we scramble
the Fifth and Sixth Regiment.

00:04:11.732 --> 00:04:12.732
No, no, no, no.

00:04:13.071 --> 00:04:15.090
This needs a much more
sophisticated mind.

00:04:15.591 --> 00:04:17.432
Someone who
understands technology.

00:04:17.472 --> 00:04:19.972
You want to send in a lab rat?
Not just any lab rat.

00:04:20.512 --> 00:04:21.792
A lab rat with teeth.

00:04:21.871 --> 00:04:23.972
You're not suggesting
who I think you're suggesting.

00:04:24.071 --> 00:04:26.071
I know,
he's a little weird.
Weird?

00:04:26.192 --> 00:04:28.611
No. No way.
He's a psychological tire fire!

00:04:28.672 --> 00:04:31.952
But he's also brilliant.
Five PhDs, IQ off the charts.

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:34.852
And his drone tech
is revolutionary!

00:04:35.092 --> 00:04:36.832
You're sure he can handle this?

00:04:37.585 --> 00:04:39.304
He has a perfect
operations record.

00:04:39.397 --> 00:04:41.117
Remember the coup in Pakistan?
No.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:42.460
Or the uprising
in Azerbaijanistan?

00:04:42.554 --> 00:04:44.398
That's not even a country.
Exactly.

00:04:44.491 --> 00:04:46.397
And you can thank
Robotnik for that.

00:04:46.872 --> 00:04:50.072
I can't believe you're
bringing that freak into this.

00:04:50.532 --> 00:04:52.212
Neither can I, but...

00:04:52.972 --> 00:04:54.311
we have no choice.

00:04:54.415 --> 00:04:56.941
[helicopters whirring]

00:05:01.677 --> 00:05:04.308
[indistinct shouts]

00:05:05.572 --> 00:05:09.676
[truck rumbling]

00:05:20.341 --> 00:05:21.381
What the...

00:05:21.482 --> 00:05:24.235
[air hissing]

